      "description": "The JUDGEMENT half of every QA verdict this instance carries across runs, split out of `test/results/` by owner ruling D2 (a), 2026-10-01 (bean `2gst`, arc `3fva`): derived script verdicts move to the `qa-reports` branch; anything a reviewer judged stays HERE, on main, where a `git rm` of derived results cannot reach it. One `qa-attestations/v1` file per subject at `<family>/<mirrored subject path>.attestations.json`, where `<family>` is the derived family it sits beside (`kg-qa`, bean `2gst`; `block-qa` and `translation-qa`, bean `8wj1`) and the mirror is exactly that family's own, so a subject's attestation is found by swapping the tree root and the suffix. Today: the `pair_attestations` that were carried inside `kg-qa/v1` sidecars, ALL of them, the `by: baseline` entries with the `by: agent` ones; the owner ruled on 2026-10-01 that a baseline is a judgement, because a regenerated one forgets the drift it recorded (defect C4). `voice_reviews` live here too when one is recorded. Under `block-qa/` and `translation-qa/`: every block or translation verdict whose `reviewer.kind` is not `script` (13 at the split, 11 + 2), held in a `criteria` map of the derived report's own shape; the derived report keeps a projection composed from here. Schema and the five read states (hit / miss / absent / corrupt / unknown): `schemas/sdlc/qa-attestations.ts`. Owner ruling 2 (2026-10-01): a writer that finds judgements in a prior derived file and no store entry MOVES them here as it saves, rather than refusing; a corrupt store is still unknown and refused. Hosted instances (bootstrap) would sit under `<stub>/`, as their `qa` verdicts do. Declared WITH its files, per bean dh4f.",
